@ GL 32 x 24, OB 14 x 2 (16 bytes a number) + 3 000 to spare, up to the thousand: MEM (the build computes it),
@ + GH 1 x 300 (GHM, 4 800) when there is no saved game (v0.6.0: 62 000 + 9 600) (the plies of CHN 0: SIGN). Old BD GL OB (a stop leaves them) freed first (0 STO): INIT makes them
@ again. Too little: a message, a key, BD GL OB deleted, your stack back, the end ("RAM is full" avoided) ----
